  "description": "The works are a combination of three areas and are described as so below:\n\nArea 1 - Garden.  Artificial Grass Installation - 62m2. This includes: Excavation to recommended depth / Installation of stabilising membranes and weed control fabric / Installation of edging around the perimeter / Aggregate installed and compacted / Blinding layer of granite dust installed and compacted / Artificial grass layed, secured and brushed / Waste removed from site / Site to be left clean and tidy. The location of this area is between the house and the church, on the inside of our premises.\n\nArea 2 & Area 3 - Parish Centre Patio 1. Work: New reinforced concrete slab (Area 2) and paving (Area 3): Area 2 RC slab approx. 65m2, Area 3 paving approx. 28.8m2. the work will include the following:\n\n• Break out and remove existing tarmac and associated unsuitable material within the proposed work areas.\n• Excavate to the required formation levels and remove arisings from site.\n• Supply, place and compact MOT Type 1 sub-base in layers.\n• Supply and install damp proof membrane to the reinforced concrete slab area.\n• Supply and install A142 mesh reinforcement, including spacers and tying wire.\n• Supply, pump, place, compact and finish C30/35 ready-mixed concrete to form an approximately 150mm reinforced slab. • Supply and install new 600 x 600 x 50mm concrete paving slabs over a prepared bedding layer.\n• Supply and install new concrete edging units to the paved area.\n• Cut, joint and clean the completed paving.\n• Remove construction waste generated by the works and leave the work area clear on completion.\n\nArea 2 will have four 7' x 7' outdoor storage sheds on this space (four in total for this area), which are made from High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE).\nArea 3 will have two 7' x 7' outdoor storage sheds on this space (two in total for this area), which are made from High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE).\n",
